2019 has passed, and we need to summarize every bit of the past year.
The top priority in 2019 is of course getting married to my wife. I vaguely remember that my wife didn’t cry at the wedding, but I cried from beginning to end...
A lot has been gained during project development:
- It is recommended to use RN as the company's core business development solution;
- Build a CI/CD continuous integration H5 (testing, production) Docker environment based on gitlab;
- Build an App-side test package output environment based on Jenkins;
- Self-built node service, provided internally by the company, applies Icon mass production service, payment code mass production service, and verification code query service;
- First year of front-end management;
Insufficient
- Insufficient coding standards practices;
- Insufficient technical depth;
- Insufficient management methods;
- Customized study plan failed to be completed.
2019 was a year of anxiety for me. I didn’t know how to learn. The endless emergence of frameworks was really dazzling. I didn’t know whether to start with basic javascript or learn a framework in depth. It was very confusing. Until the end of the year, the direction of learning was determined, focusing on the framework, learning the principles and techniques of framework implementation, and then learning in depth the native JS used in the framework.
2019 is also a year when I understand that everyone has their own ambitions. Not everyone is willing to take the initiative to learn and optimize all aspects of the project, but I will definitely find and solve problems.
2019 was also the year when I understood the product. From being furious with the product change requirements at the beginning, to patiently listening to the product, optimizing and perfecting the project over and over again.
In 2019, I saw the blogs updated by the big guys and told us a truth. If you have absolute execution and learning ability, you will also become a big boss.
In 20 years, I also set up a flag:
- I have always liked girls, and I will definitely achieve my goal of having a girl this year;
- Update a blog every week to summarize the learning content of the week;
- Dig deep into the React technology stack, from the most basic data flow, life cycle, and components to the high-level components and Hooks you are currently learning, and then to discover new continents;
- Learn swift, find an open source project, make a demo, and prepare for cross-end development.
- For me who weighs 170 pounds, it’s time to lose weight, so I’ll lose 20 pounds first…
